  /* SHORT DESKTOP — AC-PPC-HERO-ROOMS-1.2, 2026-09-06.
     WHY THIS IS STRUCTURAL AND NOT MORE SPACING. Measured from dist/ at scrollY 0, the panel's
     six in-flow rows come to 700.79px of CONTENT before a single pixel of padding or gap:
       header 73.39 · field grid 404.72 · consent 81.19 · verify 73.19 · submit 48 · microcopy 20.30
     The fold budget for the panel is V - header(73) - clearance(16) - hero padding(40):
       1440x900 -> 771 (fits, untouched below)   1536x864 -> 735 (fits)
       1280x800 -> 671 (content alone EXCEEDS by 29.79)
       1366x768 -> 639 (content alone EXCEEDS by 61.79)
     So at 1366x768 and 1280x800 the stacked panel cannot fit even with zero padding and zero
     gaps. Tightening space further is arithmetically incapable of clearing it, and the remaining
     alternatives — dropping a field, shrinking text under the readable floors, clipping, or an
     inner scroller — are all forbidden. What is left is the panel's UNUSED HORIZONTAL ROOM: the
     copy column beside it is 708px wide and only ~381px tall, and the panel itself stacks two
     full-width blocks (description, photos) and two more (verify, submit) that each leave most of
     a 528px line empty. This band pairs them. Nothing is removed, reworded, hidden or shrunk —
     every field, label, helper, the consent and the microcopy still render in full at their
     existing sizes, inputs stay >=44px tall with >=16px text, the submit stays >=48px, and
     helper/consent/microcopy stay at 14px.

     880px is the threshold because 1440x900 already passes with 22.22px of clearance and is left
     exactly as it was; the band opens just under it, at the first size that fails. */
  @media (min-width: 75rem) and (max-height: 880px) {
    /* Two panel tracks. The left is floored at Turnstile's 300px flexible-widget minimum so the
       widget never lands under its own render threshold; the right takes what is left for the
       submit. Every other row still spans both tracks. */
    .ppc-form {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 1fr) minmax(0, 224px);
      padding: 14px;
    }

    .ppc-form > * {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }

    /* The anti-spam control and the submit share ONE row instead of two. Saves the submit's own
       row plus its gap; the button keeps its full label and stretches to the widget's height, so
       it gets LARGER here, never smaller.

       Both are matched through `.ppc-form >` rather than on the class alone. Astro scopes
       `.ppc-form > *` by stamping its data attribute on BOTH sides of the combinator, which
       leaves that rule at a higher specificity than a bare `.ppc-form__verify`; the child
       combinator here restores the tie so source order decides, as intended. */
    .ppc-form > .ppc-form__verify {
